{"language": "en", "duration": 57.0, "text": "You pull out a 20-year-old bill for a coffee and it hurts! Swipe the card and nothing. This reflex has a name, the pain of paying. With cash, you see your money leave. The brain registers the loss. With a card, the transaction becomes invisible. One tap, one beep, done. In 2001, MIT researchers auctioned off tickets to a game. Those who paid by card bid nearly double. When money doesn't feel real, we agree to pay more. It's not a lack of willpower. The brain simplifies. Retailers know it. One click payment, automatic subscriptions, buy now, pay later. Everything is designed so the pain never arrives. The trap is the bill that comes later, the monthly statement, and the pain comes right back. To take back control, pay in cash for a week or withdraw a fixed amount every Monday. Make the pain visible. And you? Which expense hurts you the most?", "words": [{"word": "You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.32}, {"word": "pull", "start": 0.32, "end": 0.62}, {"word": "out", "start": 0.62, "end": 0.76}, {"word": "a", "start": 0.76, "end": 0.96}, {"word": "twenty-euro", "start": 0.96, "end": 1.64}, {"word": "bill", "start": 1.64, "end": 1.84}, {"word": "for", "start": 1.84, "end": 2.04}, {"word": "a", "start": 2.04, "end": 2.18}, {"word": "coffee", "start": 2.18, "end": 2.46}, {"word": "and", "start": 2.46, "end": 3.08}, {"word": "it", "start": 3.08, "end": 3.4}, {"word": "hurts!", "start": 3.4, "end": 4.0}, {"word": "Swipe", "start": 4.68, "end": 5.0}, {"word": "the", "start": 5.0, "end": 5.16}, {"word": "card", "start": 5.16, "end": 5.42}, {"word": "and", "start": 5.42, "end": 5.92}, {"word": "nothing.", "start": 5.92, "end": 6.2}, {"word": "This", "start": 6.7, "end": 7.0}, {"word": "reflex", "start": 7.0, "end": 7.36}, {"word": "has", "start": 7.36, "end": 7.66}, {"word": "a", "start": 7.66, "end": 7.82}, {"word": "name,", "start": 7.82, "end": 8.08}, {"word": "the", "start": 8.44, "end": 8.56}, {"word": "pain", "start": 8.56, "end": 8.